As the chief executive of this city, the mayor shall:
(1) See that all laws and ordinances of the city are faithfully executed;
(2) Preside at all meetings of the mayor and city council [sic] and have the right to take part in the deliberations of said board, but shall not vote on any question except in the case of a tie;
(3) Sign all deeds and contracts, except deeds for property sold under execution at public sale;
(4) Cosign, along with the city clerk or city manager, all checks for the payment of moneys over $1,000.00 as approved in the budget. The mayor pro tempore may cosign for the mayor in the absence from the city of the mayor. Any two of the mayor, the mayor pro tempore, the city clerk, or the city manager may cosign checks for the payment of moneys up to and including $1,000.00 or less as approved in the budget. All other payments of money, invoices, bills and vouchers must be approved by the mayor and board of aldermen and be cosigned as provided for payment of money as approved by the city budget.
(5) Keep the board of aldermen advised from time to time of the general condition of the city and recommend such measures as he or she may deem necessary or expedient for the welfare of the city;
(6) Call the board of aldermen together at any time when deemed necessary;
(7) To appoint, subject to the approval of the board of aldermen, at the first meeting of each year, or as soon thereafter as expedient, members of standing committees and such other committees as the mayor and board of aldermen may deem necessary; and
(8) Vote only in case of a tie.
(Ord. No. 91-009, § 3(2.29), 4-4-1991; Ord. No. 96-009, § 2, 3-21-1996)

